{"claims":[{"excerpt":"De POA-refunddienst: eerst aanvragers, later caseworkers","claim":"De aanpak bracht de aanvragers vóór het caseworkerwerk.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"My team focused on the users applying for refunds first and this is what we took to the alpha assessment. Plans for the caseworker user came later.","narrative":"eerst de aanvragerservaring uitwerken, later caseworkerwerk toevoegen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The title accurately summarizes the order described in the source.","materiality":"Material to the piece’s central point about the order of work."},{"excerpt":"De POA-refunddienst werd binnen twaalf weken publiek gelanceerd.","claim":"The service launched publicly within twelve weeks.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"We passed alpha and beta Service Standard assessments and launched to the public in only 12 weeks.","narrative":"Het POA-refundteam lanceerde de dienst na twaalf weken","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"This matches the source’s launch timeframe.","materiality":"Material context for the deadline and approach."},{"excerpt":"De aanvankelijk gevraagde levering binnen enkele weken werd niet haalbaar geacht als de gebruikersdienst tegelijk kwalitatief moest blijven.","claim":"The team judged the initially requested delivery in a matter of weeks infeasible if it was to deliver a quality service to users.","category":"certainty","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"We were initially asked to deliver the service in a matter of weeks, which put huge pressure on everyone and we quickly discovered would not be possible if we wanted to create a quality service for our users.","narrative":"de aanvankelijk gevraagde termijn van enkele weken niet haalbaar werd geacht met behoud van een kwalitatieve gebruikersdienst","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The Dutch accurately preserves both the initial request and the condition that quality be maintained.","materiality":"Material context for the team’s time pressure."},{"excerpt":"De aanvragerservaring werd eerst naar alpha gebracht.","claim":"The applicant-facing experience was taken to alpha first.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"My team focused on the users applying for refunds first and this is what we took to the alpha assessment.","narrative":"eerst de aanvragerservaring uitwerken","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"This is a faithful rendering of which users’ needs were addressed first at alpha.","materiality":"Central to the described sequencing."},{"excerpt":"Plannen voor caseworkers kwamen later.","claim":"Plans for caseworkers came later than the applicant-focused work.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Plans for the caseworker user came later.","narrative":"later caseworkerwerk toevoegen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"Directly stated in the source.","materiality":"Central to the described sequencing."},{"excerpt":"Tijdens de private beta wisselden tweewekelijkse sprints af tussen aanvragen aannemen en tijd besteden aan testen, onderzoek en verwerking.","claim":"During private beta, fortnightly sprints alternated between accepting applications and time for testing, research, and processing.","category":"chronology","label":"F1 minor immaterial imprecision","evidence":"We achieved this by splitting our fortnightly sprints in two: testing, researching and accepting applications in the first week and then suspending submissions to concentrate on testing, researching and processing applications the second.","narrative":"tijdens de private beta vaste tijd reserveren voor onderzoek en testen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The summary captures the sprint rhythm and activities but omits the precise division: applications were accepted in the first week, while submissions were suspended in the second; testing and research occurred in both.","materiality":"The omitted week-by-week detail does not materially change the account of the work rhythm."},{"excerpt":"Zo bestond de beschreven werkwijze onder tijdsdruk uit een volgorde waarin aanvragers eerst kwamen, met daarnaast expliciet gereserveerde tijd voor onderzoek en testen.","claim":"The team’s described approach under time pressure combined prioritizing applicants first with explicitly allocated research and testing time.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"My team focused on the users applying for refunds first and this is what we took to the alpha assessment. Plans for the caseworker user came later.","narrative":"De beschreven aanpak combineerde een volgorde waarin aanvragers eerst kwamen met expliciet gereserveerde tijd voor onderzoek en testen.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"This is a fair synthesis of the source’s sequencing and its planned split of fortnightly sprints for testing and research. The source also describes the delivery request as putting huge pressure on the team.","materiality":"This is the piece’s central characterization of the approach."},{"excerpt":"Dat beschrijft de aanpak van het POA-refundteam;","claim":"The described choices characterize this team’s approach rather than a universal method.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Here are a few of my top tips:","narrative":"Presenteer dit als de werkwijze van dit team, niet als een bewezen recept.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The piece frames the practices as this team’s approach, not a general rule. The source offers personal tips, while the upstream guidance specifically cautions against making this approach universal.","materiality":"Important scope constraint that avoids generalizing from one team’s experience."},{"excerpt":"het stelt op zichzelf niet vast dat die aanpak de lancering of de resultaten heeft veroorzaakt.","claim":"The source does not establish that the approach caused the launch or the reported results.","category":"cause","label":"F2 material incorrect, unsupported or misleading","evidence":"This was key to us being able to build the service so quickly while ensuring it met user needs.","narrative":"zonder ze als bewezen oorzaak van de lancering of resultaten voor te stellen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source does not link the approach to the reported five-week metrics, but it does explicitly attribute the ability to build the service quickly to the sprint arrangement. The blanket wording that the approach is not established as causing the launch therefore suppresses a material causal attribution made by the source. It would be accurate to say the source does not establish that the approach caused the reported results.","materiality":"Material because the causal caveat contradicts the source’s stated relationship between the sprint arrangement and building the service quickly."}]}

